From: XTU MUSA bring-up
Subject: [PATCH] qwen4_exp: route MUSA to the Triton/AMD path

This is a candidate patch against vLLM v0.32.0; it is NOT validated on MUSA.
It only fixes platform dispatch.  The AMD path still contains CUDA-specific
PDL/GDC calls that need separate guards.

diff --git a/vllm/models/qwen4_exp/__init__.py b/vllm/models/qwen4_exp/__init__.py
--- a/vllm/models/qwen4_exp/__init__.py
+++ b/vllm/models/qwen4_exp/__init__.py
@@ -26,7 +26,10 @@ def __getattr__(name: str) -> Any:
         if current_platform.is_xpu() or current_platform.is_tpu():
             raise NotImplementedError("Qwen4Exp currently supports CUDA and ROCm only")
-        if current_platform.is_rocm():
+        is_musa = getattr(current_platform, "is_musa", lambda: False)()
+        if current_platform.is_rocm() or is_musa:
             from .amd.model import (
                 Qwen4ExpForCausalLM,
                 Qwen4ExpForConditionalGeneration,
